  "source_scope_note": "The selected problem is Theorem 4.1: every rational-equivalence orbit of an effective degree-k zero-cycle on a complex abelian variety has dimension at most k-1. The complete author body retains all local orbit notation, Mumford-form reduction and the entire required infinitesimal dimension Proposition 4.2, including torus degeneration, coordinatewise product, algebraic-curve and Laurent-pole arguments. Mumford theorem and elementary algebraic-group/Grassmannian facts remain named prerequisites; gonality, very-general countability, Chow-ring and other orbit assertions are unselected context.",
